147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 99 0 R
/T (This report presents the work carried out during my internship as a Market Research Analyst Intern in the real estate sector. The main objective of my internship was to conduct market research to help the company evaluate the feasibility of establishing a customer lounge near the airport. During the internship, I was assigned the responsibility of studying passenger movement around the airport and understanding the demand for lounge facilities. The company wanted to know how many passengers arrive at the airport, how many of them use nearby lounges, and whether there is enough demand for a new lounge in that location. To complete this task, I conducted detailed market research using both primary and secondary sources. I visited areas around the airport, observed customer movement, collected information about existing lounges, and gathered data related to passenger traffic and customer preferences. I also analyzed the facilities offered by nearby lounges and studied factors such as location, pricing, occupancy, and customer convenience. After collecting the required information, I organized the data, analyzed the findings, and prepared a report with useful insights. The research helped identify the potential demand for a new airport lounge and highlighted the factors that influence customers when choosing lounge services. This internship provided me with practical exposure to market research, data collection, data analysis, and report preparation. It also improved my communication, observation, analytical thinking, and problem-solving skills. Working on a real business problem helped me understand how market research supports decision-making in the real estate industry. Overall, the internship was a valuable learning experience that allowed me to apply theoretical knowledge in a practical environment while gaining a better understanding of the real estate market and customer behavior.)
/E (This report presents the work carried out during my internship as a Market Research Analyst Intern in the real estate sector. The main objective of my internship was to conduct market research to help the company evaluate the feasibility of establishing a customer lounge near the airport. During the internship, I was assigned the responsibility of studying passenger movement around the airport and understanding the demand for lounge facilities. The company wanted to know how many passengers arrive at the airport, how many of them use nearby lounges, and whether there is enough demand for a new lounge in that location. To complete this task, I conducted detailed market research using both primary and secondary sources. I visited areas around the airport, observed customer movement, collected information about existing lounges, and gathered data related to passenger traffic and customer preferences. I also analyzed the facilities offered by nearby lounges and studied factors such as location, pricing, occupancy, and customer convenience. After collecting the required information, I organized the data, analyzed the findings, and prepared a report with useful insights. The research helped identify the potential demand for a new airport lounge and highlighted the factors that influence customers when choosing lounge services. This internship provided me with practical exposure to market research, data collection, data analysis, and report preparation. It also improved my communication, observation, analytical thinking, and problem-solving skills. Working on a real business problem helped me understand how market research supports decision-making in the real estate industry. Overall, the internship was a valuable learning experience that allowed me to apply theoretical knowledge in a practical environment while gaining a better understanding of the real estate market and customer behavior.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
